#: kaccess.cpp:366
msgid "Slow keys is now enabled."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:367
msgid ""
"This may be because you hold down the Shift key for 8 seconds or because "
"some application has enabed this feature.\n"
"You can configure slow keys and similar features in the Regional & "
"Accessibility->Accessibility module of the KDE Control Center.\n"
"To quickly disable slow keys, press the Shift key for another 8 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:375
msgid "Bounce keys is now enabled."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:376
msgid ""
"This may be because some application has enabed this feature.\n"
"You can configure bounce keys and similar features in the Regional & "
"Accessibility->Accessibility module of the KDE Control Center."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:382
msgid "Sticky keys is now enabled."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:383
msgid ""
"This may be because you pressed the Shift key 5 consecutive times or because "
"some application has enabed this feature.\n"
"You can configure sticky keys and similar features in the Regional & "
"Accessibility->Accessibility module of the KDE Control Center.\n"
"To quickly disable sticky keys, press the Shift key for another 5 times."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:391
msgid "Mouse keys is now enabled."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:394
msgid ""
"This may be because some application has enabed this feature.\n"
"You can configure mouse keys in the Peripherals->Mouse module of the KDE "
"Control Center."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:398
msgid ""
"This may be because you pressed %1 or because some application has enabed "
"this feature.\n"
"You can configure mouse keys in the Peripherals->Mouse module of the KDE "
"Control Center.\n"
"To quickly disable mouse keys, press %2 again."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:407
msgid "Multiple AccessX features have been enabled."
msgstr ""

#: kaccess.cpp:408
msgid ""
"This may be because some application has enabed these features.\n"
"You can configure them in the Regional & Accessibility->"
"Accessibility module of the KDE Control Center."
msgstr ""

